---
layout: default
---
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/resources.css' | relative_url }}">
<div class="resource-notebook">
  <header class="notebook-header">
    <p class="notebook-kicker">Swathi’s field notes / Open resources</p>
    <h1>
      A few useful<br>
      starting points.
    </h1>
    <p>Coursework I’ve worked through, lessons from applying, and places to look for research. Take what helps; make it your own.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="notebook-layout">
    <nav class="notebook-index" aria-label="Resource chapters">
      <span>In this notebook</span><a href="#coursework">01 / Coursework</a><a href="#grad-guide">02 / Grad applications</a
      ><a href="#checklist">03 / Your checklist</a><a href="#opportunities">04 / Research opportunities</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="notebook-content">
      <section id="coursework" class="notebook-chapter">
        <p class="notebook-kicker">01 / From my undergrad</p>
        <h2>Learn by doing.</h2>
        <p>Assignments, implementations, problem sets, and reports from electrical engineering and computing at IIT Madras.</p>
        <a class="notebook-text-link" href="https://github.com/BaristaBandits/Undergrad_Courses">Browse the complete repository ↗</a>
        <div class="course-index">
          {% for course in site.data.resources.courses -%}
            <a class="course-row" href="{{ course.url | escape }}"
              ><span class="course-number">0{{ forloop.index }}</span
              ><span
                ><strong>{{ course.title | escape }}</strong><span>{{ course.description | escape }}</span
                ><small>{{ course.files }} files in the repository</small></span
              ><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
            >
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="notebook-note">These links contain coursework and assignments. My separate lecture-note collection is not currently available.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="grad-guide" class="notebook-chapter">
        <p class="notebook-kicker">02 / Finding your next step</p>
        <h2>A graduate application field guide.</h2>
        <p>
          Distilled from the notes I collected while figuring out applications. A practical way to organize the process, with room for your own
          priorities.
        </p>
        <div class="guide-sections">
          {% for section in site.data.resources.guide %}
            <details
              {% if forloop.first %}
                open
              {% endif %}
            >
              <summary>
                <span>0{{ forloop.index }}</span>{{ section.title | escape }}
              </summary>
              <p>{{ section.text | escape }}</p>
            </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="notebook-note">
          Program websites are the source for current requirements. This guide uses a relative sequence rather than the dates and score targets in my
          original notes.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="checklist" class="notebook-chapter">
        <p class="notebook-kicker">03 / Make it yours</p>
        <h2>A little less to keep in your head.</h2>
        <p>Use this checklist as you prepare. When browser storage is available, your progress stays on this device.</p>
        <div data-application-checklist>
          <p class="checklist-progress" data-checklist-progress role="status" aria-live="polite">
            0 of {{ site.data.resources.checklist.size }} steps complete
          </p>
          {% for item in site.data.resources.checklist -%}
            <label class="notebook-check"
              ><input type="checkbox" value="{{ item.id }}"><span>{{ item.text | escape }}</span></label
            >
          {%- endfor %}
          <button class="notebook-reset" type="button" data-checklist-reset hidden>Reset checklist</button>
          <p class="notebook-note" data-checklist-storage></p>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section id="opportunities" class="notebook-chapter">
        <p class="notebook-kicker">04 / Follow your curiosity</p>
        <h2>Where to look for research.</h2>
        <p>
          A directory drawn from my earlier internship search. Explore the official websites for the current application cycle, research fit,
          eligibility, and funding.
        </p>
        <p class="notebook-note">
          The original tracker was for 2025. Its deadlines and application statuses are not reproduced here; listing a program does not mean it is
          currently accepting applications.
        </p>
        <div class="opportunity-tools" data-opportunity-tools hidden>
          <label>Find a program<input type="search" data-opportunity-search placeholder="Program, institution, or research area…"></label
          ><label
            >Location<select data-opportunity-region>
              <option value="all">All locations</option>
              <option>USA</option>
              <option>Switzerland</option>
              <option>Multiple locations</option>
            </select></label
          >
        </div>
        <p class="notebook-note" data-opportunity-count role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="opportunity-directory">
          {% for program in site.data.resources.programs %}
            <article class="opportunity-row" data-opportunity data-region="{{ program.region | escape }}">
              <div>
                <span class="opportunity-region">{{ program.region | escape }}</span>
                <h3>
                  <a href="{{ program.url | escape }}">{{ program.title | escape }} ↗</a>
                </h3>
                <p>{{ program.institution | escape }} · {{ program.area | escape }}</p>
              </div>
              <a class="notebook-text-link" href="{{ program.url | escape }}">Official website</a>
            </article>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p data-opportunity-empty hidden>No programs match. Try a broader search or another location.</p>
        <a class="notebook-download" href="{{ '/assets/resources/research-opportunities.csv' | relative_url }}" download
          >↓ Take the directory with you (CSV)</a
        >
        <p class="notebook-note">Includes blank columns for current deadlines, eligibility, requirements, and your notes.</p>
      </section>
      <footer class="notebook-footer">
        Collected along the way. Shared for the next person.<a href="{{ '/projects/' | relative_url }}">Explore my research ↗</a>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/resources.js' | relative_url }}" defer></script>
